Gen-data prompt attribution and license notices

The finite protected-input editing and restoration sequence in
internal/ui/gendata_prompt.go is adapted from HighLine 3.1.2, by
James Edward Gray II and Greg Brown, specifically:

  lib/highline.rb (ask/say/get_line)
  lib/highline/question.rb
  lib/highline/question_asker.rb
  lib/highline/terminal.rb
  lib/highline/terminal/io_console.rb

Original distribution: https://github.com/JEG2/highline

Copyright 2005 Gray Productions. All rights reserved.
Copyright 2006 Gray Productions. All rights reserved.
This is Free Software. See LICENSE and COPYING for details.

This port selects HighLine's Ruby software license option. It translates only
the gen-data question sequence into synchronous injected Go callbacks. Labels
are literal, without ERB; successful answers remain raw for the authentication
owner. Reached ordinary answers require UTF-8, deletion removes one codepoint,
and explicit EOF/result contracts distinguish echoed and protected input.
Restoration uses an acquired callback, including partial entry failure, rather
than assuming echo=true. There is no native terminal/backend implementation,
stream ownership transfer, worker, general validator, menu or masking facility.

